+- ENTRY WIRING: `TestCustodyAncestorWalkReachableFromProductionEntries` mechanically confirms Probe, Spawn, and Execute reach `CheckSocketCustody` and the same `checkCustodyAncestors` predicate.
+- TRANSITIVE GUARD: `TestCustodyAncestorWalkHasNoLengthDependentControlFlow` derives the active in-module call graph from the ancestor predicate and checks every reachable decision callee for path-derived length/depth branches and counters. It includes `custodyModeForPath`, `writableByOthers`, `isFilesystemRoot`, and `secprim.OpenNoFollowDir` plus local callees. The mechanically discovered `memberErrorTarget` exception is used only for `failPath` details.
