 ## 2026-09-24
 
+### TASK-260830-g0pcnt rework rev6 — physical path-depth bound
+
+- PATH DOMAIN: The walk-length fixture now reaches `unix.PathMax-1` instead of stopping at a selected test depth. On Darwin the generated runtime-root path is 1023 bytes, with 452 one-byte nested directories and 460 ancestor positions. `TestCustodyAncestorWalkGeneratedDepthToPathMax` plants mode 0777 at the deepest and middle non-root ancestors and asserts the literal `tmux_unsafe_socket_path` refusal. The deep derived socket exceeds `sun_path`, so the physical-depth test drives the shared predicate directly.
+- ENTRY WIRING: `TestCustodyAncestorWalkReachableFromProductionEntries` mechanically confirms Probe, Spawn, and Execute reach `CheckSocketCustody` and the same `checkCustodyAncestors` predicate.
+- TRANSITIVE GUARD: `TestCustodyAncestorWalkHasNoLengthDependentControlFlow` derives the active in-module call graph from the ancestor predicate and checks every reachable decision callee for path-derived length/depth branches and counters. It includes `custodyModeForPath`, `writableByOthers`, `isFilesystemRoot`, and `secprim.OpenNoFollowDir` plus local callees. The mechanically discovered `memberErrorTarget` exception is used only for `failPath` details.
+- MUTANTS: `N-ancestor-walk-callee-depth-cap-24` is killed by the PATH_MAX test; `N-ancestor-walk-filesystem-root-depth-cap` is killed by the transitive AST guard. Each ran alone twice, with raw subprocess exit 1 in each run. The applied line-count-preserving `C-control` survived. The focused suite passed in `rev6-focused-tests-04.log`.
+- BOUNDS: The earlier B44, B46, and N2 bounds remain unchanged. No tmux process or real socket is required. The full rev6 357-row mutant harness has not run; the prior complete 355-row pass is carried only for unchanged rev5 plants.
+
 ### TASK-260830-g0pcnt rework rev5 — generated custody depth closes the rev4 repeat-of
 
 - FINDING: Rev4 found custody walk length pinned to fixture depth. The generated-depth test varies 1–16 extra nested levels and places a non-sticky 0777 ancestor at the nearest, middle, and deepest non-root position through Probe, Spawn, and Execute: 144/144 named refusals, zero effects. The path oracle now covers 22 component positions across current and extra-depth-08 fixtures and all three entries: 270,336/270,336 low-mode classifications, 330/330 kind cases, 54/54 owner cases. The rev5 mode/kind/owner fixtures use the shared production predicates through production entry wiring.
